Subject: Uldaros Theorix: let the AI cast it (its ETB stays unused)
Why: The ETB is a chain of DB$ Pump steps that pick up to one card of each type in the
  graveyard. PumpAi refuses a Pump with nothing to aim at, and its sub-ability check ignores
  AILogic$ Always, so AiController.checkETBEffects rejected the trigger and with it the creature:
  the deck's 6-drop sat in hand (Dimir Uldaros, baseline: seen in 188 games, cast in 3). Even
  when cast, the refusing steps left no targets, so the AI never cast anything from the
  graveyard. OptionalDecider$ You makes the trigger optional (same outcome as choosing no
  targets), so the AI casts Theorix as a 5/5 flier and declines the ETB as before. Making the
  AI use the ETB would need Java (PumpAi target selection for graveyard "choose" steps).
Measured: `mtgsim gauntlet decks/standard/meta/dimir-uldaros.txt --vs <the other ten meta decks> -n 100
  --seed 1`, default AI, Forge 7db198d72e, on 13 Nov 2026. Arm without patches: 30.1% (95% CI
  27-33%, 301-699). Arm with 0006 and 0007 together (separate shares not measured): 33.9%
  (31-37%, 339-661). Difference +3.8 points, 95% CI -0.3 to +7.9, p = 0.07: not a reliable
  change on 1,000 games each. Mirror on the patched engine (`match dimir-uldaros dimir-uldaros
  -n 200 --seed 1`): 51.0% (44-58%).
  Uldaros Theorix cast in 326 of 632 games where it was seen (13 of 616 without).

